abstract: >-
  wafer-proc-sim is an open-source framework for 4H-SiC blade dicing
  process optimization. The core contribution is a data-quality-aware
  heteroscedastic Gaussian process surrogate trained on curated
  experimental chipping data (N=25; Grade A/B subset N=11 achieves
  LOO RMSE 1.62 µm, R² 0.80 vs 3.12 µm / 0.34 for mixed-quality data).
  The pipeline integrates Ensemble Kalman Filter blade-wear tracking and
  Bayesian recipe optimization. Reproducible via scripts/reproduce_paper.sh
  with CI-regression-tested metrics. Extension modules cover semiconductor
  equipment physics (TEL, Keyence, DISCO) for portfolio demonstrations.

